From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: hostapd measured the signal, so read it

Every backhaul link in the mesh reported its signal as "unknown" while
hostapd had the number all along.

A 4-address (WDS) backhaul station is attributed to its AP/VLAN child
netdev, so nl80211 GET_STATION on the AP-MLD netdev yields nothing for it
and rssi_avg stays 0. rssi_to_rcpi(0) is 255 - the spec's not-available
value - so the controller stored 255 for every bSTA and anything choosing a
path by signal was choosing on nothing.

iface_get_sta_info_band() already consults hostapd unconditionally for
exactly this reason ("hostapd ctrl is authoritative"), and
hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_info() already parses flags, listen interval and
the whole capability set out of that same reply. It just never read the one
line that was missing.

Measured 2026-09-07 on the corridor node, both backhaul children:

  wifi.apmld.ap-mld-2 stations       rssi 0        both STAs, both links
  wifi.ap.ap-mld-2 stations          rssi 0        both STAs
  hostapd sta <mac>                  signal=-46    signal=-56
  iw dev ap-mld-2 station get <mac>  -46 dBm       -56 dBm
  iw dev ap-mld-2.staN station dump  -48 dBm       -56 dBm

The driver and hostapd agree; only the library came back empty.

Filled only when nl80211 left it at zero, so a driver that does report the
signal keeps what it reported. Per-chain rssi[] is untouched: hostapd gives
one aggregate figure and inventing a per-antenna breakdown from it would be
the same class of defect this fixes.

Verify: on a mesh with a wireless backhaul, sta.rcpi for each bSTA on the
controller must show a real value instead of 255, and it must agree with
`iw dev <backhaul-ap> station get <bsta>`.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/hostapd_ctrl.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/hostapd_ctrl.c
@@ -197,6 +197,37 @@
 
 #endif
 
+/* hostapd measured it; read it.
+ *
+ * A 4-address (WDS) backhaul station is attributed to its AP/VLAN child
+ * netdev, so GET_STATION on the AP-MLD netdev returns nothing for it and
+ * rssi_avg stays 0. rssi_to_rcpi(0) is 255, the not-available value - so
+ * every backhaul link in the mesh reported "unknown" for its signal while
+ * hostapd had the number the whole time.
+ *
+ * Measured 2026-09-07 on the corridor node, two backhaul children:
+ *
+ *   wifi.apmld.ap-mld-2 stations      rssi 0        (both, both links)
+ *   hostapd sta <mac>                 signal=-46 / -56
+ *   iw dev ap-mld-2 station get <mac> -46 dBm / -56 dBm
+ *
+ * This is only ever a fill-in: a driver that does report the signal has
+ * already written it, and is not touched.
+ */
+static int hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_signal(const char *buf, int8_t *rssi_avg)
+{
+	char val[256] = { 0 };
+
+	if (!rssi_avg)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	if (wpa_ctrl_get_param(buf, "signal", val, sizeof(val)))
+		return -1;
+
+	*rssi_avg = (int8_t)strtol(val, NULL, 10);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_listen_interval(const char *buf, uint16_t *listen_int)
 {
 	char val[256] = { 0 };
@@ -939,6 +970,10 @@
 	hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_listen_interval(buf, &info->listen_int);
 	hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_flags(buf, sta_flags, sizeof(sta_flags));
 
+	/* Only when nl80211 left it empty - see the helper for why it does. */
+	if (info->rssi_avg == 0)
+		hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_signal(buf, &info->rssi_avg);
+
 	if (strstr(sta_flags, "[HT]")) {
 		size_t mcs_len = sizeof(info->caps.ht.supp_mcs);
 		info->caps.valid |= WIFI_CAP_HT_VALID;
